Cell[TextData[{
 "Calls TriangulateMesh and returns {MeshCoordinates[mesh], \
plaquettePositions}, with cells converted to selectors suitable for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Extract"]], "paclet:ref/Extract"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->{"InlineFormula"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "389167af-6c27-d94a-b3a3-02a68ef6d59c"],
 " in ChernNumberByWilsonLoop."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->1176534424,ExpressionUUID->"028e793f-a8b8-0347-b11e-e86d50ef7b46"],

Cell["\<\
For a two-dimensional triangular mesh, a plaquette with coordinate indices \
i,j,k is represented as {{i,j,k}}.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->633273309,ExpressionUUID->"0b766c63-f48c-ba4b-9af7-5e5158e4e98f"],

Cell["\<\
The default MaxCellMeasure is {d -> RegionMeasure[region] 0.1^d}, where d = \
RegionDimension[region]. TriangulateMesh options are accepted and Method -> \
\"ConstrainedQuality\" is supplied internally.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1914544745,ExpressionUUID->"8f9ab6ef-d23a-a449-98d7-3d314e94540d"],

Cell["\<\
The function also Echoes a mesh visualization labelled with vertex and \
plaquette counts. Its one-dimensional branch combines all cell indices into a \
single selector.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1883731035,ExpressionUUID->"f9dcf0eb-0dbb-6346-88e0-e42462dfcae6"]
}, Closed]],

